 - Rooms, users, bookings and amenities endpoints.
 - Pagination on list endpoints.
 - Conflict detection when creating a booking.
+
+## Unreleased
+
+- Booking conflict detection covers every overlap, not only the ones starting
+  inside an existing booking.
+- The slot check and the write run in one transaction, so two simultaneous
+  requests can no longer take the same slot.
+- Bookings that end before they start, or that start in the past, are refused.
+- Bookings pointing at an unknown room or user answer 404 instead of 500.
+- `PATCH /bookings/:id` validates the booking it produces instead of writing
+  the change unchecked.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 9fcd23c..4fa650f 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -17,3 +17,17 @@ make demo-data  # load sample rows for local browsing
 ```
 
 The API listens on the port given by `PORT`, default 3000.
+
+## Booking rules
+
+A booking request is refused when:
+
+- it ends before it starts, or lasts no time at all (`400 VALIDATION_ERROR`);
+- it starts in the past (`400 VALIDATION_ERROR`);
+- its room or its user does not exist (`404 NOT_FOUND`);
+- its period overlaps an active booking of the same room (`409 BOOKING_CONFLICT`,
+  with the offending booking in `details.conflictingBookingId`).
+
+Periods that merely touch — one starting exactly when the other ends — do not
+overlap. Cancelled bookings hold no slot. `PATCH /bookings/:id` is checked
+against the booking the patch produces, under the same rules.
